  "worked_solution": "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{1}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} & =2([{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}]-{x}_{2}^{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2})-{x}_{2}^{2} & =2({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n2{y}_{1}^{2}-3{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $3\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}.$",
